      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "322775b06ff570130cac0ef49e1f61f8b2344aca",
            "subject": "LU-21061 lod: keep MDT pool members apart from OSTs"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Di Wang",
          "email": "diwa@nvidia.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 18:56:05.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Di Wang",
          "email": "diwa@nvidia.com",
          "date": "2026-11-21 04:22:13.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21061 mgs: allow adding MDTs to pools",
        "message": "LU-21061 mgs: allow adding MDTs to pools\n\nlctl pool_add and the MGS accept only OST names, so a pool cannot\nlimit which MDTs a directory tree uses.\n\nAccept MDT names in check_and_complete_ostname() and\nmgs_pool_check_ostname(), checking them against the MDT index map.\nRefuse MDT0000 in the MGS with -EPERM: it holds the root and the\nfilesystem-wide services, so it is never part of a pool.  Print \"MDT\"\ninstead of \"OST\" in the lctl messages for MDT members.\n\nOn an MDS, llapi reads pool members from a local LOD, which now lists\nMDTs too, but it assumes a pool has no more members than there are\nOSTs: llapi_get_poolmembers() prints the \"Pool:\" header again when its\ncaller retries with a larger buffer, and print_obd_quota() prints\nnothing for such a pool.  Print the header only once the members are\nread, and size the pool quota list for OSTs and MDTs, skipping the\nMDTs.\n\nClients keep ignoring MDT members until they learn about them.\n\nTest-Parameters: forjanitoronly\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I45a544461d3ed7e2b273c16e8f871785082cce20\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
